- [ ] Performance Improvements
  - [ ] suggestLinks reads the whole links table (~474ms at 77k) because the backlog
    filter (unread / un-slushed / non-resource, priority-ordered) has nothing
    indexable. A compound [priority, added_at] index would let it stop early.
  - [ ] tagsByRecentUse reads all 61k link_tags (~399ms) to order ~120 tags by most
    recent use. A `last_used_at` column on the tag row makes it a 120-row read, but
    that is a data-model change: migration + sync.go + sync tests.
- [ ] Make the terms used to strip tracking configurable. Keep the same default list, but allow people to specify other query params to strip if they want to
- [ ] I noticed previously when adding links that have a `'` in them that the auto-titling (in the backend) it breaks (e.g. if a page is titled `it doesn't matter your rank`, I would get `it doesn` back as the page title), make sure everything is escaped properly in responses and on any ingest for the auto-titling. I can't remember if this was already fixed previously or not, so just verify and fix if necessary
